{"question": "What are the key considerations for a controlled system maintenance program?", "framework_version": "rev5", "answer_text": "A controlled system maintenance program must address the information security aspects of maintenance and apply to all types of maintenance on system components conducted by local or nonlocal entities, including peripherals such as scanners, copiers, and printers. Key considerations include: ensuring maintenance records contain necessary details (such as the date and time, a description of the maintenance, names of those performing the maintenance, the name of the escort, and system components removed or replaced) and considering supply chain-related risks associated with replacement components.", "answer_text_with_citations": "A controlled system maintenance program must address the information security aspects of maintenance and apply to all types of maintenance on system components conducted by local or nonlocal entities, including peripherals such as scanners, copiers, and printers. Key considerations include: ensuring maintenance records contain necessary details (such as the date and time, a description of the maintenance, names of those performing the maintenance, the name of the escort, and system components removed or replaced) and considering supply chain-related risks associated with replacement components.

