{"question": "What does MP-6 require for sanitizing media prior to disposal or release?", "framework_version": "rev4", "answer_text": "MP-6 requires sanitizing media prior to disposal or release by employing sanitization mechanisms with the strength and integrity commensurate with the security category or classification of the information.", "answer_text_with_citations": "MP-6 requires sanitizing media prior to disposal or release by employing sanitization mechanisms with the strength and integrity commensurate with the security category or classification of the information.

Citations: mp-6_smt, mp-6_gdn (NIST SP 800-53 Rev. 4)", "evidence_spans": [{"source_id": "mp-6_smt", "span_text": "The organization: a. Sanitizes {{ insert: param, mp-6_prm_1 }} prior to disposal, release out of organizational control, or release for reuse using {{ insert: param, mp-6_prm_2 }} in accordance with applicable federal and organizational standards and policies; and b. Employs sanitization mechanisms with the strength and integrity commensurate with the security category or classification of the information."}, {"source_id": "mp-6_gdn", "span_text": "This control applies to all information system media, both digital and non-digital, subject to disposal or reuse, whether or not the media is considered removable. Examples include media found in scanners, copiers, printers, notebook computers, workstations, network components, and mobile devices. The sanitization process removes information from the media such that the information cannot be retrieved or reconstructed. Sanitization techniques, including clearing, purging, cryptographic erase, and destruction, prevent the disclosure of information to unauthorized individuals when such media is reused or released for disposal. Organizations determine the appropriate sanitization methods recognizing that destruction is sometimes necessary when other methods cannot be applied to media requiring sanitization. Organizations use discretion on the employment of approved sanitization techniques and procedures for media containing information deemed to be in the public domain or publicly releasable, or deemed to have no adverse impact on organizations or individuals if released for reuse or disposal. Sanitization of non-digital media includes, for example, removing a classified appendix from an otherwise unclassified document, or redacting selected sections or words from a document by obscuring the redacted sections/words in a manner equivalent in effectiveness to removing them from the document. NSA standards and policies control the sanitization process for media containing classified information."}], "status": "OK", "odp_required_list": [], "ask_list": [], "primary_citation": "mp-6_smt", "all_citations": "mp-6_smt, mp-6_gdn", "contract_mode": "generative_rag_baseline", "debug": {"query_plan": {"original_query": "What does MP-6 require for sanitizing media prior to disposal or release?", "rewrites": ["What are the requirements specified in MP-6 for sanitizing media before disposal or release?", "What technical standards does MP-6 outline for sanitizing media intended for disposal or release?", "MP-6 what measures are necessary for sanitizing media prior to disposal or release?"]}, "retrieval_meta": {"base_margin_ratio": 0.017244532221490864, "base_top1": "MP-6", "base_top2": "MP-6(1)", "bm25_top1": null, "dense_top1": null, "final_margin_ratio": 0.23636025190353394, "final_top1": "MP-6", "n_docs": 35, "num_variants": 4, "ranked_controls": ["MP-6", "MP-6(1)", "MP-8(4)", "MP-6(7)", "MP-8(3)", "MP-6(3)", "MP-7(2)", "MP-4", "MP-6(8)", "MP-8", "MP-5", "MP-6(2)", "MP-7", "MP-1", "MP-3", "MP-2", "MP-8(1)", "MP-4(2)", "MP-5(3)", "MP-7(1)", "MP-5(4)", "MA-3(3)", "SA-19(3)", "CP-6(1)", "MA-5(1)", "MP-8(2)", "PS-6", "MA-6(1)", "MA-2", "PE-6(3)", "SC-34(2)", "PE-6(4)", "PE-16", "AU-9(1)", "CP-6", "SC-6", "MA-3(2)", "PS-6(2)", "PS-6(3)", "AC-3(9)", "CM-2(7)", "AU-10(4)", "MA-4(3)", "SA-12(14)", "AU-6(9)", "CP-6(2)", "CP-7(6)", "MA-6(2)", "CM-6", "CP-6(3)"], "rerank_alpha": 0.65, "rerank_applied": true, "rerank_apply_min_margin_ratio": 0.15, "rerank_effective_apply_min_margin_ratio": 0.1, "rerank_margin_ratio": 0.23636025190353394, "rerank_skip_min_base_margin_ratio": 0.1, "rerank_skip_require_top1_agreement": false, "rerank_top1": "MP-6", "reranker_called": true, "selected_clause_ids_by_control": {"MP-4": ["mp-4_smt", "mp-4_smt.b", "mp-4_smt.a", "mp-4_gdn"], "MP-5": ["mp-5_smt.a", "mp-5_smt", "mp-5_smt.c", "mp-5_smt.d", "mp-5_smt.b", "mp-5_gdn"], "MP-6": ["mp-6_smt", "mp-6_smt.a", "mp-6_gdn